  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Handling the Quota Issue**\n\nI\'ve hit a quota limit with the image generation. No worries, I\'m pivoting to the fallback plan as instructed. Right now, I\'m thinking about using `picsum.photos` for placeholder images, but I\'m also questioning if we can utilize SVG illustrations or icons.\n\n\n**Prioritizing SVG Implementation**\n\nNow, I\'m fully committed to building the UI and logo directly with React SVGs. This offers unparalleled control for hover effects, animations via Framer Motion, and theming, all in a crisp, scalable, responsive design. The clean paths and fine gradients are the perfect fit for a top-tier visual identity in a blue & white palette. I\'m focusing on crafting an SVG-based logo and gorgeous UI sketches in React/CSS using Tailwind, to ensure robustness and high performance. Plus, no more broken external image URLs! I\'m making sure to address the goals and scope rules: high conversion, good user experience, responsive design in blue and white, showcasing Spacevip Sistemas, services, testimonials, and a contact form, and using TypeScript.\n\n\n**Designing the Core Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core feature set. The plan is a minimalist, sticky header and a captivating hero section with an interactive ERP/dashboard mockup and lead capture widget. I\'ll also add a chatbot-style AI assistant using Gemini, called \"Spacevip AI,\" to provide system category suggestions, recommended modules, tech stack options, and complexity estimations based on user input.\n\n\n**Showcasing the Value**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Services/Solutions\" section with grid cards and premium icons, dynamically expanding on hover, for ERP/CRM customization, process automation, high-performance web portals, and API integration. Then, a step-by-step interactive map will reveal the Spacevip methodology, moving through discovery, architecture, development, and delivery. Finally, I\'ll feature client success testimonials with measurable metrics.\n\n\n**Refining Lead Capture**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the lead form, aiming for high conversion. It\'s multi-step, validating input and storing details locally. Gemini is being employed to create personalized tech outlines and present instant, stunning proposals to the user! I\'m planning to persist user form data with Firestore as the system grows.\n\nI\'m also considering a toggleable or hidden client inquiry dashboard for submitted projects.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Engagement**\n\nI\'m now integrating a detailed client panel within the webpage to track submitted requests in real-time. It will simulate a \"Consultant Review Status,\" updating interactively. This engaging feature, using local persistence with `localStorage`, aims for higher conversion. I need to ensure the Gemini client calls are server-side and plan to implement an Express + Vite server-side route for secure proxying. I must update the scripts in `package.json` to support a custom `server.ts` build.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `/src/types.ts` file to define structured TypeScript interfaces, types, and constants that our frontend and backend will share. This ensures strong type safety and clean organization."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 785352178
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
