    thinking: "**Designing the App Core**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the core of the application within `/src/App.tsx`. I\'ve started meticulously planning the integration of the `AIAssistant` and `DashboardMockup` components. This central component will need to orchestrate their interactions and manage the flow of data.\n\n\n**Crafting the Contact Form**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual design and layout for the `ContactForm`. I\'m starting by designing a premium SVG logo: a futuristic orbital sphere intersected with a cyber network in gradient blues and cyans, alongside bold \"SPACEVIP\" text. Following this, I\'m structuring a gorgeous landing section with a dynamic navbar and hero section. The hero section is planned with a column layout to emphasize unique systems and integrate an interactive `DashboardMockup`.\n\n\n**Developing the Simulated Interface**\n\nI\'m now deeply engaged in crafting the simulated corporate interface within the `DashboardMockup`. Specifically, I\'m integrating several key sections. I\'ve designed a horizontal stats bar with `OFFICE_STATS`, displaying prominent blue values. Also, I\'m embedding the `AIAssistant` chat within the interface, styled with high contrast. I\'m also planning the Services section\'s grid, and the Process Section\'s vertical timeline.\n\n\n**Refining the App Layout**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `ContactForm` into `/src/App.tsx`, focusing on its role as a proposal blueprint calculator. Also, I\'m working on an interactive FAQs section using custom accordion cards to boost conversion rates. Finally, I\'m designing a responsive and elite footer to match the design. I\'ve double checked icon licensing, opting for Lucide Icons for their broad availability. We\'re now reviewing the codebase for imports of React hooks, Lucide Icon renderers, custom components, and static arrays.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now implement the complete main layout inside `/src/App.tsx`. It features:\n1. A floating glassmorphism header with a futuristic corporate inline SVG logo.\n2. A hero area pairing our main high-conversion value statement with the interactive `DashboardMockup`.\n3. Clear high-impact stats with custom micro-animations.\n4. An interactive **Services/Solutions Explorer** matching the user\'s specific services, with a collapsible drawer system revealing target modules and specific ROI metrics.\n5. Our **Interactive Process timeline** showing the structured development lifecycle.\n6. The interactive model consultation panel (`AIAssistant`) and our highly converting custom proposals blueprint generator (`ContactForm`).\n7. An interactive FAQ accordion solving common technical sales objections to maximize client conversion rates.\n8. Solid, clean footer and WhatsApp integration."
