  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Database Architecture**\n\nI\'m focusing on building the database module. My initial thought is to create a database manager module at `/server/db.ts` to manage the PostgreSQL connection. I\'m planning to construct the connection string using...\n\n\n**Refining Database Connection**\n\nI\'m now refining the database connection strategy. I\'m prioritizing environment variables (PGHOST, PGPORT, PGUSER, PGPASSWORD, PGDATABASE) for the PostgreSQL credentials. If those are unavailable, I\'ll default to the user-provided credentials (`spacevip_site`, `spacevip_react`, `Jo159357*`). Also, I will add an asynchronous retry system to handle connection failures gracefully, falling back to a memory or file-based database for development. This fallback ensures a robust and interactive developer experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Interaction**\n\nI\'m now implementing the database interaction logic within `/server/db.ts`. I\'ve defined the `Contact` interface and am writing the `getContacts`, `saveContact`, and `updateContactStatus` functions. I\'m also including an `initDb` function to manage database initialization. Furthermore, I\'ll be adding an admin dashboard that clearly displays the connection status, whether to the live PostgreSQL or the secure local backup, for transparency.\n\n\n**Defining Database Operations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating the table within the database, handling both connected and JSON fallback scenarios. I\'m leveraging the `Inquiry` interface defined in `/src/types.ts` for data representation. Specifically, I\'m now writing `/server/db.ts`, and considering how to manage database operations within that file, but I need to ensure compliance with the file directory structure.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 976467814
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
